WHO   — The Four Houses — money, women, food, and cheating death
WHAT  — The powers Garth plays against each other: four corrupt vices given thrones, the order the stranger dismantles from within.
WHERE — ARN · Arena  Framework inputs: Arena (Forstchen, 1994)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the city's rot needs faces — four greedy Houses whose feuds Garth turns into their undoing.
HOW   — By wealth, lust, gluttony, and the fear of dying — each House a vice, each a duelist in the Arena.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  We were four Houses of fighter-mages, each ruled by a different greed — and the one-eyed stranger needed only to let our greeds collide.

